: "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release recorded as healthy, in all production regions. The rollback reports v2.3.0 running in us-east, us-west, and eu-west, with execution state VERIFIED. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is fixed. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-promoting.", "confidence": 0.93, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release recorded as healthy. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release that was running everywhere, with an error rate of 0.18. The v2.3.1-rc build was only in staging.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-ups. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI did not re-check the service status after the rollback, so error-rate recovery is not confirmed yet. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}